From: Stephan Zehrer <stephan@zehrer.net>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: eth: r8152: receive into a 16 KiB buffer

The RTL8152 and RTL8153 pack Ethernet frames that arrive close together
into one bulk IN transfer (RX aggregation, which the driver enables). The
driver reads that transfer into a 2048-byte buffer, so as soon as two
full-size frames arrive back to back the device sends more than the host
asked for. The host controller reports a babble error and both frames are
lost:

  Rx: failed to receive: -5

On a Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W with an RTL8152 HAT (DWC2 host) an image
download over HTTP fails after a few KiB, and TFTP with the default
1468-byte blocks after a few dozen KiB. Only TFTP with 512-byte blocks
gets through, at a few KB/s.

Raise RTL8152_AGG_BUF_SZ to 16 KiB. The receive buffer, the bulk IN
transfer length and the RX early size of the RTL8153 all derive from it,
so the device's aggregation limit and the buffer stay in step.

---
 drivers/usb/eth/r8152.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/eth/r8152.h b/drivers/usb/eth/r8152.h
--- a/drivers/usb/eth/r8152.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/eth/r8152.h
@@ -500,7 +500,7 @@
 #define BYTE_EN_END_MASK	0xf0
 
 #define RTL8152_ETH_FRAME_LEN	1514
-#define RTL8152_AGG_BUF_SZ	2048
+#define RTL8152_AGG_BUF_SZ	16384
 
 #define RTL8152_RMS		(RTL8152_ETH_FRAME_LEN + CRC_SIZE)
 #define RTL8153_RMS		(RTL8152_ETH_FRAME_LEN + CRC_SIZE)
